  "goodToKnow": "Der Mindestlohn is the minimum wage. Germany only introduced a national, legal Mindestlohn on 1 January 2015, at 8.50 euros an hour; before that, wages were set by collective agreements between unions and employers. A commission now proposes regular increases. Mindest- means minimum, from mindestens (at least). Der Lohn is wages, usually for hourly or manual work, while das Gehalt is a salary."
